<title>USA: FPL St Lucie 1 power output drops to 7 pct.</title>
<headline>FPL St Lucie 1 power output drops to 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity production at Florida Power &amp; Light's (FPL) 839 megawatt (MW) St Lucie 1 nuclear power plant has dropped to seven percent, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The unit had been operating at full capacity Friday.  </p>
<p>The NRC, in its daily status report, said the unit's production had been cut to balance the main turbine.</p>
<p>The plant is one of two 839 MW units at FPL's Hutchinson Island, Fla., facility.</p>
<p>No other details were immediately available.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk + 1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
